{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And Yitzhak loved Esav.</b> Concerning Yitzhak it is written <b>ויאהב</b> (with vav conversive), to teach you that Yitzhak did not love him constantly but only at that time — <b>for game was in his mouth</b> — whereas concerning Yaakov, who was a wholesome man, it is written of him <b>ורבקה אהבת את יעקב</b>, constant love. And furthermore, it is a woman's way to love one who tends her flocks."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:56.145499624Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}